            <ArticleTitle>Pleomorphic adenoma of the nasal septum.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>210-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pleomorphic adenoma may occur in any site in which there is salivary gland tissue. It has rarely been described arising in the nasal cavity. We report a case of septal pleomorphic adenoma and discuss the clinical presentation and surgical management.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
